WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.220
A library shelf, labelled:
critics on this poem.

2
00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.370
It's completely empty.

3
00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:09.480
On the desk, a single poem glows.

4
00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:13.480
It was written this century, and
nobody has written about it yet.

5
00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:17.420
No critics, no essays,
no ready-made readings.

6
00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:19.710
So how do you write about it?

7
00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:23.190
In this mission, you'll ask
what an examiner can reward,

8
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.300
when there's no critic to quote.

9
00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:31.360
You'll set an old ode beside a new one:
"Thou still unravish'd bride of quietness,"

10
00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:33.920
and ask what the new one does with it.

11
00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:36.710
And you'll test yourself
on an invented poem,

12
00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:40.350
set at a supermarket
self-checkout, late at night.

13
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:45.180
Your mission: work out how to write
about a poem no critic has touched.
